-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      1.0 played by Jon Attree in JNext through the real loader,
              2026-11-03; 1.1 played by the owner in JNext on NextZXOS v2.10
              (System/Next 26.11), 2026-11-06: approved

  Replay      1.1: NexClash's ROM path check (nextboot.rom_paths) on the v2.10
              ROM3, 7 recordings, 194456 frames: the ROM bytes the game runs
              are the same as on v2.09 (1.0: BEEPER 0x03C1-0x03C4 differs in
              all 7). 1.0: 2 bot recordings from this file, 30000 frames:
              IDENTICAL, 5575 helicopter plots, 1012910 sprite pixels.
              Negative controls 6/6 detected. Dean's recordings desync on this
              file at once

  Emulator    1.1, 2026-11-06: JNext 1.1.104 headless, through the Browser and
              the real loader on System/Next 26.11 (NextZXOS v2.10) and on
              v2.09: reached play, keys answered, beeper sound in the recorded
              audio, /tmp/NEXCLASH.NEX equal to apply; 1.0 on 26.11: hangs at
              the start of play (BEEPER runs into RAM). 1.0: JNext 1.1.104
              headless: plain and sprites reach play, nobody played; with the
              loading screen: JNext 1.1.104 headless through the real loader,
              MD5 exact, reached the screen, the game and play frames, viewed;
              no person played it; JNext 1.1.104 headless through the real
              loader, 2026-11-03: chosen in the Browser with every cheat on,
              /tmp/NEXCLASH.NEX equal to apply

  Coverage    1.1 changes only the start-up stub: after its copy of the
              running ROM3 into the alt ROM it puts v2.09's bytes back at 11
              sites where that ROM3 holds v2.10's (BEEPER, PLOT, POINT, DRAW,
              CIRCLE); on v2.09 nothing changes; POINTERS (0x1664) is left as
              v2.10 has it. 1.0: No aircraft in the replays (unit cases only),
              no cyclone, crates, landing or game over. About 35 code and data
              bytes differ from the engine's own snapshot, including two INC
              HL at 0x81EF and 0x81F6 that are NOP here; loading screen stub
              added in bank 14, 2026-11-03: the replay and hardware lines are
              of the build without it, whose game memory the stub restores at
              the original start; the stub is emulator-tested only; cheats
              proved in a simulator on the original game: Infinite lives:
              simulator (Kempston wander, seed 1): INC A at 92A0 runs at each
              crash; 3 helicopters lost and game over by frame 2853 without,
              none lost with; Infinite time: simulator (idle, 15000 frames):
              time tick 8295 runs 11 times; time-bar pointer steps 12 times
              without, held with; Infinite fuel: simulator (pulsed climb,
              lives held, 20000 frames): fuel bar steps in 43 of 49 in-flight
              ticks without, 0 of 58 with; post-crash drain loop exits (no
              hang), game over still reached without the lives harness; Immune
              to cyclone: simulator (seed 1, lives held, 20000 frames):
              cyclone buffet routine 7378 runs 41 frames (4 push-downs)
              without; 0 with, though in range 129 frames; No crashes:
              simulator (3 key schedules, 8000 frames): crash flag 7505 never
              set and no helicopter lost with; 3 lost in each without (frames
              shots/cy_nocrash.png: still flying at 5000)

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
